  "instance_name": "Christianity",
  "label": "Christianity",
  "description": "The meme relies on the foundational beliefs of Christianity, particularly the idea that Jesus Christ's death and resurrection are central to the faith. The image of Jesus on the cross is a powerful symbol in Christianity, representing sacrifice, redemption, and the triumph of good over evil. The message 'they can't kill the message' is interpreted by many Christians as referring to the enduring nature of the Gospel message, which is believed to be eternal and unchangeable. Understanding this requires knowledge of Christian theology and history.",
